<p>Claude Cowork is built for multi-step knowledge work rather than simple question-and-answer chats. It can plan a task, work through files and web research, and return a finished result while you review the work.</p>
<p><strong>How do you use Claude Cowork?</strong> Open Claude on a supported surface, select Cowork in the message box, describe the outcome you want, and review Claude's approach before it runs. Start with a clear goal, give only the files and access it needs, and check the result before using it.</p>
<figure class="article-image"><img src="/assets/images/blog/claude-cowork-2026.svg" alt="Abstract Claude Cowork workspace illustration"></figure>
<h2>What Claude Cowork is designed to do</h2><p>Cowork uses the same agentic architecture that powers Claude Code, but it targets knowledge work without requiring a terminal. It can handle research, file organization, document creation and other tasks that need several steps instead of one reply.</p>
<h2>Who can use Claude Cowork</h2><p>Anthropic currently lists Cowork for paid Pro, Max, Team and Enterprise plans. Availability differs by surface and organization settings, so the option may appear on desktop, web or mobile at different times.</p>
<h2>How to start a Cowork task</h2><ol><li>Open Claude on the web, desktop or mobile app where Cowork is available.</li><li>Select <strong>Cowork</strong> in the message box.</li><li>Describe the finished outcome, not just the first step.</li><li>Review the plan and permissions, then let the task run.</li></ol>
<h2>Give Cowork the right context</h2><p>A good task states the goal, source material, constraints, output format and checks. For example, instead of saying “organize these files,” specify the folder, the naming rule, the files to keep, the final structure and the report you expect at the end.</p>
<h2>When to use cloud and local access</h2><p>Cowork sessions can run in Anthropic's cloud, which lets work continue when you close your laptop. Tasks that need local files, local browser access or computer use still depend on the Claude Desktop app and the access you grant it.</p>
<h2>A simple prompt structure that works</h2><p>Use five parts: goal, inputs, constraints, deliverable and verification. Add a final check such as “show me what changed and list anything you could not verify.” This makes a long agent task easier to review.</p>
<h2>What is changing for browser use</h2><p>Anthropic is rolling out a built-in browser in Claude Desktop. It can open sites, read pages, click, type and fill forms. Claude also warns that signed-in sites and write actions need care, because an agent with more access can create larger mistakes.</p>
<h2>How to use Cowork safely</h2><p>Keep permissions narrow, connect only the folders required for the task, and avoid giving an agent access to secrets it does not need. Review write actions and important outputs before relying on them, especially for financial, legal or business-critical work.</p>
<h2>How Cowork fits with Claude Research</h2><p>Cowork is better thought of as an execution layer for larger tasks, while Claude Research is focused on structured research. You can combine them: use research to gather evidence, then use Cowork to turn the verified material into a document, spreadsheet or organized project.</p>
<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>Is Claude Cowork available on free plans?</h3><p>Anthropic currently lists Cowork for paid Pro, Max, Team and Enterprise plans.</p><h3>Can Cowork keep working when I close my laptop?</h3><p>Cloud Cowork sessions can continue on Anthropic's servers after you close your laptop. Local file and computer access still depend on the Desktop app connection.</p><h3>Can Claude Cowork use a browser?</h3><p>Yes. Anthropic documents browser use in Cowork, including a built-in browser in Claude Desktop that is rolling out gradually.</p>
